1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,960
Hi everyone! I'm Ria.

2
00:00:03,960 --> 00:00:12,310
Here are some photos of morning, afternoon, evening, and dawn.

3
00:00:12,310 --> 00:00:19,060
Which of these times do you like the most?

4
00:00:19,060 --> 00:00:22,530
When is your favorite time?

5
00:00:22,530 --> 00:00:27,070
Today, let's talk about routines.

6
00:00:27,070 --> 00:00:35,430
Let's talk about which time of day we like best.

7
00:00:35,430 --> 00:00:37,180
Morning

8
00:00:37,180 --> 00:00:41,230
What time do you wake up?

9
00:00:41,230 --> 00:00:44,370
What time do you usually wake up?

10
00:00:44,370 --> 00:00:50,900
Do you wake up early? Or do you wake up late, a bit late?

11
00:00:50,900 --> 00:00:56,260
I wake up early if I have class.

12
00:00:56,260 --> 00:01:01,490
If I don't have class, I wake up late.

13
00:01:01,490 --> 00:01:10,490
I wake up early when there's class, and late when there isn't.

14
00:01:10,490 --> 00:01:13,150
When I have class,

15
00:01:13,150 --> 00:01:17,940
I wake up around 8 or 9 in the morning.

16
00:01:17,940 --> 00:01:24,030
When I don't have class... what time do I wake up?

17
00:01:24,030 --> 00:01:25,890
Don't be surprised.

18
00:01:25,890 --> 00:01:30,240
I usually wake up at 11:00.

19
00:01:30,240 --> 00:01:33,930
11:00? Around 11:00.

20
00:01:33,930 --> 00:01:36,570
I wake up around 11:00 AM.

21
00:01:36,570 --> 00:01:40,570
Sometimes I wake up even later.

22
00:01:40,570 --> 00:01:45,340
The time I wake up is different every day.

23
00:01:45,340 --> 00:01:54,020
So, I usually don't eat breakfast.

24
00:01:54,020 --> 00:01:58,650
I eat breakfast together with lunch.

25
00:01:58,650 --> 00:02:03,430
In Korean, there's a word called 'Ajeom'.

26
00:02:03,430 --> 00:02:09,530
It means eating breakfast and lunch together.

27
00:02:09,530 --> 00:02:16,830
After eating, I sit at my desk.

28
00:02:16,830 --> 00:02:20,320
I make a plan for the day.

29
00:02:20,320 --> 00:02:22,020
I make a plan.

30
00:02:23,170 --> 00:02:28,320
I write my plan in a planner.

31
00:02:28,320 --> 00:02:30,340
I write my plan.

32
00:02:30,340 --> 00:02:33,310
I write down what I have to do today.

33
00:02:33,310 --> 00:02:39,290
The things I have to do today, it's like a 'to-do list'.

34
00:02:39,290 --> 00:02:42,600
I write down the things I need to do.

35
00:02:42,600 --> 00:02:43,780
Afternoon

36
00:02:43,780 --> 00:02:54,460
After I eat lunch, I study languages.
The first thing I do is Duolingo.

37
00:02:54,460 --> 00:02:59,200
But how do you feel after eating?

38
00:02:59,200 --> 00:03:03,100
I get so sleepy after I eat.

39
00:03:03,100 --> 00:03:07,330
I'm the sleepiest during lunchtime.

40
00:03:07,330 --> 00:03:10,640
So I doze off.

41
00:03:10,640 --> 00:03:16,070
I hold my phone like this and... doze off.

42
00:03:16,070 --> 00:03:17,470
To doze off

43
00:03:17,470 --> 00:03:21,390
After studying languages, I work.

44
00:03:21,390 --> 00:03:22,330
I work.

45
00:03:22,330 --> 00:03:23,990
I teach classes.

46
00:03:23,990 --> 00:03:28,120
My classes end in the evening.

47
00:03:28,120 --> 00:03:34,060
After class is over, I eat dinner.

48
00:03:34,060 --> 00:03:38,460
What do you guys eat for dinner?

49
00:03:38,460 --> 00:03:41,660
Do you cook and eat at home?

50
00:03:41,660 --> 00:03:44,020
Ingredients at home

51
00:03:44,020 --> 00:03:51,320
Cooking and eating with ingredients at home is called 'jip-bap'.

52
00:03:51,320 --> 00:03:52,820
Home-cooked meal

53
00:03:52,820 --> 00:03:57,370
Someone might ask you this:

54
00:03:57,370 --> 00:04:01,130
"What did you eat for dinner?"

55
00:04:01,130 --> 00:04:08,460
Then you can say, "Oh, I just had a home-cooked meal today."

56
00:04:08,460 --> 00:04:13,970
"I just had home-cooked food today." You can say it like that.

57
00:04:13,970 --> 00:04:21,410
Do you usually eat at home? Or do you eat out?

58
00:04:21,410 --> 00:04:23,520
Do you eat out?

59
00:04:23,520 --> 00:04:27,840
Eating out is called 'oesik'.

60
00:04:27,840 --> 00:04:30,200
Eating out

61
00:04:30,200 --> 00:04:33,730
Do you eat out often?

62
00:04:33,730 --> 00:04:39,230
I usually eat a home-cooked meal for lunch.

63
00:04:39,230 --> 00:04:44,730
But for dinner, I usually eat out.

64
00:04:44,730 --> 00:04:46,110
I eat out.

65
00:04:46,110 --> 00:04:48,640
I eat outside.

66
00:04:48,640 --> 00:04:51,330
I don't know why.

67
00:04:51,330 --> 00:04:57,310
I always, always want to eat spicy food.

68
00:04:57,310 --> 00:05:02,210
I love Tteokbokki and Ramen so much.

69
00:05:02,210 --> 00:05:08,220
But you shouldn't eat spicy food too often!

70
00:05:08,220 --> 00:05:12,380
Eating it often is not good for your health.

71
00:05:12,380 --> 00:05:20,910
So sometimes I eat out, and sometimes I eat a healthy home-cooked meal.

72
00:05:20,910 --> 00:05:24,640
After eating, I rest for a bit.

73
00:05:24,640 --> 00:05:26,320
I rest.

74
00:05:26,320 --> 00:05:30,310
After resting, I go to exercise.

75
00:05:30,310 --> 00:05:33,890
I go to the gym to work out.

76
00:05:33,890 --> 00:05:39,340
There are many people at the gym in the evening.

77
00:05:39,340 --> 00:05:42,340
There are so many people.

78
00:05:42,340 --> 00:05:43,700
Evening

79
00:05:43,700 --> 00:05:48,930
At night, I usually edit videos.

80
00:05:48,930 --> 00:05:54,580
We often call 'dong-yeongsang' just 'yeongsang'.

81
00:05:54,580 --> 00:05:57,500
I edit videos.

82
00:05:57,500 --> 00:05:58,740
Editing

83
00:05:58,740 --> 00:06:02,840
I really concentrate when I edit.

84
00:06:02,840 --> 00:06:04,990
I focus intensely.

85
00:06:04,990 --> 00:06:09,340
I close the door to my room.

86
00:06:09,340 --> 00:06:10,780
I shut it tight.

87
00:06:10,780 --> 00:06:16,760
'Datda' is just closing it normally.

88
00:06:16,760 --> 00:06:22,980
'Dat-a-beorida' has a much stronger feeling.

89
00:06:22,980 --> 00:06:27,260
I close my door and focus on editing.

90
00:06:27,260 --> 00:06:28,640
Timer

91
00:06:28,640 --> 00:06:33,090
I set a timer.

92
00:06:33,090 --> 00:06:35,290
I set the time.

93
00:06:35,290 --> 00:06:39,450
During that time, I only focus on editing.

94
00:06:39,450 --> 00:06:41,710
I only edit.

95
00:06:41,710 --> 00:06:45,600
After I finish editing, I wash up.

96
00:06:45,600 --> 00:06:47,390
Face

97
00:06:47,390 --> 00:06:51,710
I wash my face and brush my teeth.

98
00:06:51,710 --> 00:06:53,990
I brush my teeth.

99
00:06:53,990 --> 00:06:57,430
I take a shower.

100
00:06:57,430 --> 00:06:58,780
Hair

101
00:06:58,780 --> 00:07:03,370
I wash my hair.

102
00:07:03,370 --> 00:07:08,010
And then, what do I do with my hair?

103
00:07:08,010 --> 00:07:11,290
My hair is wet.

104
00:07:11,290 --> 00:07:19,860
I dry my hair.
Then I feel so good.

105
00:07:19,860 --> 00:07:27,200
This is my favorite time of the entire day.

106
00:07:27,200 --> 00:07:32,570
I feel great when I wash up after finishing all my work.

107
00:07:32,570 --> 00:07:39,040
As I mentioned, I wrote a plan in my planner this morning.

108
00:07:39,040 --> 00:07:45,770
I feel so good when I complete all those plans.

109
00:07:45,770 --> 00:07:52,580
How do I feel if I can't finish the plan?

110
00:07:52,580 --> 00:07:57,110
To be honest, I don't feel very good.

111
00:07:57,110 --> 00:08:00,750
Anyway, now it's night.

112
00:08:00,750 --> 00:08:01,340
Night

113
00:08:01,340 --> 00:08:07,680
After I'm all washed up, I play chess at night.

114
00:08:07,680 --> 00:08:12,230
I play two games of chess a day.

115
00:08:12,230 --> 00:08:13,660
Two games

116
00:08:13,660 --> 00:08:16,030
I only play exactly two games.

117
00:08:16,030 --> 00:08:20,190
I try to play only two games.

118
00:08:20,190 --> 00:08:22,130
I try

119
00:08:22,130 --> 00:08:27,790
If I play more, I might go to bed late.

120
00:08:27,790 --> 00:08:33,010
What time do you guys usually go to sleep?

121
00:08:33,010 --> 00:08:42,330
I want to go to sleep around 12:00 AM.

122
00:08:42,330 --> 00:08:46,980
But I fail every single day.

123
00:08:46,980 --> 00:08:51,040
So... it becomes dawn.

124
00:08:51,040 --> 00:08:52,550
Dawn

125
00:08:52,550 --> 00:08:57,850
How many games did I say I play?

126
00:08:57,850 --> 00:09:02,970
I said I play only two games.

127
00:09:02,970 --> 00:09:06,620
But sometimes I play more.

128
00:09:06,620 --> 00:09:09,370
Why do I play more?

129
00:09:09,370 --> 00:09:10,929
Why?

130
00:09:10,929 --> 00:09:15,191
I lost both of the games.

131
00:09:15,191 --> 00:09:19,123
Then I can't fall asleep.

132
00:09:19,123 --> 00:09:21,609
I feel so bummed that I can't sleep.

133
00:09:21,609 --> 00:09:25,441
I can't sleep because it's so frustrating.

134
00:09:25,441 --> 00:09:28,650
So I play one more game. Again!

135
00:09:28,650 --> 00:09:29,560
I lose again.

136
00:09:29,560 --> 00:09:31,350
Then what happens?

137
00:09:31,350 --> 00:09:34,480
I play one more.

138
00:09:34,480 --> 00:09:37,790
It's not gambling.

139
00:09:37,790 --> 00:09:41,570
Time just flows by like this.

140
00:09:41,570 --> 00:09:44,710
Time flies so fast.

141
00:09:44,710 --> 00:09:47,940
But! It's not like this every day.

142
00:09:47,940 --> 00:09:51,940
Please don't misunderstand.

143
00:09:51,940 --> 00:10:00,540
Like I said before, I really want to sleep early.

144
00:10:00,540 --> 00:10:09,470
And ideas! Suddenly at dawn, many ideas pop up.

145
00:10:09,470 --> 00:10:10,820
Pop up

146
00:10:10,820 --> 00:10:14,910
So that's when I write scripts.

147
00:10:14,910 --> 00:10:17,730
I write video scripts.

148
00:10:17,730 --> 00:10:22,070
I write down ideas in a notebook.

149
00:10:22,070 --> 00:10:25,080
I write in this notebook.

150
00:10:25,080 --> 00:10:29,410
These are characters I really like.

151
00:10:29,410 --> 00:10:31,870
A cat and a mouse.

152
00:10:31,870 --> 00:10:38,020
Anyway, when is my favorite time?

153
00:10:38,020 --> 00:10:39,390
It's night.

154
00:10:39,390 --> 00:10:40,620
Night

155
00:10:40,620 --> 00:10:42,190
I mentioned it earlier, right?

156
00:10:42,190 --> 00:10:51,190
I like it best when I've done all my work and just finished washing up.

157
00:10:51,190 --> 00:10:54,960
I like it most when I've just come out from washing up.

158
00:10:54,960 --> 00:10:59,190
Morning, afternoon, evening, night.

159
00:10:59,190 --> 00:11:05,440
Out of these, which is your favorite time?

160
00:11:05,440 --> 00:11:09,730
I think it will be very different for everyone.

161
00:11:09,730 --> 00:11:11,810
So I'm curious.

162
00:11:11,810 --> 00:11:19,140
Try thinking about your day right now.

163
00:11:19,140 --> 00:11:20,260
To think of

164
00:11:20,260 --> 00:11:23,770
Are you a diligent person?

165
00:11:23,770 --> 00:11:27,840
Or are you more of a relaxed person?

166
00:11:27,840 --> 00:11:29,730
Diligent

167
00:11:29,730 --> 00:11:38,620
Diligent people wake up early, go to bed early, and always live busily.

168
00:11:38,620 --> 00:11:39,970
Living busily.

169
00:11:39,970 --> 00:11:41,470
Relaxed

170
00:11:41,470 --> 00:11:48,620
Being relaxed means not being busy and being comfortable.

171
00:11:48,620 --> 00:11:56,250
In my view, there are many diligent people in Korea.

172
00:11:56,250 --> 00:12:02,860
But everyone has a different lifestyle pattern.

173
00:12:02,860 --> 00:12:07,060
There is no right answer.

174
00:12:07,060 --> 00:12:11,170
As long as you are happy, that's what matters.

175
00:12:11,170 --> 00:12:18,430
I hope you felt happy while listening to this podcast today.

176
00:12:18,430 --> 00:12:20,890
I hope you were happy.

177
00:12:20,890 --> 00:12:27,260
I am filming this video at 7:00 right now.

178
00:12:27,260 --> 00:12:31,140
7:00 AM? 7:00 PM?

179
00:12:31,140 --> 00:12:34,250
I'm filming at 7:00 PM.

180
00:12:34,250 --> 00:12:45,470
So, like I said earlier, I'm going to wash up, play chess, and go to sleep.

181
00:12:45,470 --> 00:12:47,450
How many games of chess?

182
00:12:47,450 --> 00:12:51,140
I'll sleep after playing exactly two games.

183
00:12:51,140 --> 00:12:58,850
You guys should also organize your day after listening to this video!

184
00:12:58,850 --> 00:13:00,770
To organize

185
00:13:00,770 --> 00:13:02,340
Try organizing your day.

186
00:13:02,340 --> 00:13:06,010
What time do you wake up and go to bed?

187
00:13:06,010 --> 00:13:09,270
What is your favorite time?

188
00:13:09,270 --> 00:13:12,720
Please practice a lot in the comments.

189
00:13:12,720 --> 00:13:22,660
Also, other example sentences for today's words and audio files are on Patreon.

190
00:13:22,660 --> 00:13:24,540
Go check them out.
